course: dictionary
lesson: 11059
title: Weekly: once every week
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Weekly means something happens once every week. Look at the words around it for clues: «weekly pocket money» tells you the money comes once a week, and a «weekly spelling test» is a test every week. Check by swapping in "once a week" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Weekly can describe a thing, like a «weekly shop», or tell you how often something happens, like «paid weekly». It can also mean "for one week", so a weekly amount is the amount for seven days.
explain: Weekly can be a noun too. «A weekly» is a newspaper or magazine that comes out once a week. Ask yourself whether the word is a thing or an action in the sentence, and that will show you which meaning fits.
fact: Weekly means once every week.
fact: «Weekly» can also mean for one week, as in «weekly pocket money».
fact: «A weekly» is a newspaper or magazine that comes out once a week.
fact: «Twice weekly» means two times every week.
fact: In maths, a weekly amount is the amount for one week: you can multiply it by the number of weeks, or divide by 7 to find one day.
exercise: «Some months have 4 weeks and some have 5, so money paid weekly does not always add up to the same as money paid monthly.» What does paid weekly mean? | Paid in coins | Paid once every year | Paid only on one day | *Paid once every week
exercise: Mum says, "We do the weekly shop on Saturdays." What is the weekly shop? | *A big shop done once every week | A shop open for one hour | A shop that sells only magazines | A shop for birthday cards
exercise: «A music chart is a weekly list of the most popular songs.» What does weekly tell you about the list? | It has only one song in it | It is made by one judge once a year | *It is made once every week | It is a list of songs sung at night
test: «She buys a weekly about horses.» What is a weekly here? | *A magazine that comes out once a week | Something you do every day | A horse | A race
test: Which word means once every week? | *weekly | hourly | daily | yearly
exam: «The Sabbath is the weekly day of rest.» What does weekly mean here? | Happening at night | Happening once every hour | Happening only once in a whole life | *Happening once every week
